# Shared by both Dockerfiles — they build from the same context, so models/
# (COPYed by the app image) and hailo-rt-4/ (COPYed by the base image) must both
# stay. Listed below is everything neither image COPYs.
#
# This is not a build-context size optimization: BuildKit transfers only the
# files a COPY actually resolves, so the measured context is already minimal
# (~16 MB for the base image build — just the two HailoRT packages). What it
# buys instead: nothing unreferenced can be dragged in by a future COPY or a
# widened wildcard, .DS_Store and __pycache__ never reach the image, and a
# non-BuildKit builder — which does send the whole context — skips .git.
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
# A leading ** is required to match at depth — a bare *.pyc matches root-level
# files only, it does not cross a /.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
*.pyo
**/*.pyo

docs/
tests/
scripts/
setup.sh
*.md
**/*.md
LICENSE
